25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems the human element is shifting; we have plenty of coders now, but the phenotyping experts have vanished into industry.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've noticed that while some costs are rising, the ministry is still helping us with glasshouse subsidies and computing hours.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Oh no! The spectroscopy suite was broken for eleven weeks! But the animal facility is doing great with new vet cover.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears that field sites are quite volatile due to disasters, and biological colonies cause far more delays than simulations.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data suggests that broad catalogues have a much longer lasting impact than specific mechanism studies, which often stall.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,A sobering thought. We must ensure the project we pick has the actual hands available to do the work.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Midori,,I agree. We should consider which projects rely on those stable subsidies versus the volatile costs.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Kenji,,We definitely shouldn't pick something that needs that broken spectroscopy machine right now!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. The risk profile of live colonies versus computation is a critical variable for our timeline.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"We should prioritize the type of research that historically delivers a tangible, lasting resource.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
