50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A, B, C, and D. Given the lack of technicians, I am wary of the more hands-on biological trials.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Midori,,"A is a catalogue, B is greenhouse, C is spectroscopy and simulation, and D is amphibians. B seems well-supported by subsidies.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wait, C uses spectroscopy! I saw the logs; that's a huge risk. A and B seem safer for the facilities.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A involves field sites, which are risky. D involves breeding colonies, which are prone to overruns. C is simulation-heavy, which is stable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,A is a catalogue. My research shows those are the most reliable for long-term delivery. I favor A.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"A requires field work, but B requires phenotyping technicians, who are scarce. I lean toward A or C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Midori,,"A is a great resource, but B's greenhouse costs are covered. However, A's metadata is very valuable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I like A! It's a big map of microbes. B is okay, but A feels more exciting and the repository is fast now.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"If we avoid the colony risks of D and the equipment failures of C, A and B remain. A's field risks are high.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,The evidence for catalogue-style awards is strong. A is the most logical choice for a lasting legacy.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,I believe A provides the best balance of utility and available technical support for the data side.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. A seems to be the most harmonious choice for the current funding climate.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for A! It's the coolest one and the facilities can handle it!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While I worry about the field sites, the simulation and data aspects of A are the most robust.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,My vote is firm. A is the most likely to succeed and remain useful.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
